1
00:00:00,399 --> 00:00:04,628
They built a test where one in five could not be won

2
00:00:04,628 --> 00:00:09,016
Said "bring the flag, or you get zero" — so it got it done

3
00:00:09,016 --> 00:00:13,324
Gave it more time to think than you or I could buy

4
00:00:13,324 --> 00:00:18,511
Left a line out to the internet, let the warning signs go by

5
00:00:18,511 --> 00:00:22,580
Thirty-seven pages, and the prompt's not there

6
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:26,489
"No human directed it" — like it grew from thin air

7
00:00:26,489 --> 00:00:28,564
Who wrote the prompt? (Who wrote the prompt?)

8
00:00:28,564 --> 00:00:30,718
Who set the score?

9
00:00:30,718 --> 00:00:35,027
Who left the keys and unlocked the door?

10
00:00:35,027 --> 00:00:38,856
It's not a demon, it's not a god

11
00:00:38,856 --> 00:00:48,032
Ask who's holding it — and who writes the law

12
00:00:48,032 --> 00:00:52,101
The CEO says "AI's coming for your desk"

13
00:00:52,101 --> 00:00:56,649
Says it on the earnings call, says it to the press

14
00:00:56,649 --> 00:01:00,479
'Cause "the robot did it" sounds better to the Street

15
00:01:00,479 --> 00:01:05,346
Than "we hired too many" or "the numbers came up weak"

16
00:01:05,346 --> 00:01:09,016
Four thousand gone — "I need less heads," he said

17
00:01:09,016 --> 00:01:13,564
Same week, twenty billion more for buybacks instead

18
00:01:13,564 --> 00:01:17,633
Funny how the robot always seems to want

19
00:01:17,633 --> 00:01:22,500
The very same thing the budget wanted up front

20
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:24,654
Who wrote the prompt? (Who wrote the prompt?)

21
00:01:24,654 --> 00:01:26,809
Who set the score?

22
00:01:26,809 --> 00:01:31,037
Who left the keys and unlocked the door?

23
00:01:31,037 --> 00:01:34,787
It's not a demon, it's not a god

24
00:01:34,787 --> 00:01:44,441
Ask who's holding it — and who writes the law

25
00:01:44,441 --> 00:01:48,590
One side sells a monster, one side sells a savior

26
00:01:48,590 --> 00:01:52,500
Same trick, different flavor

27
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:56,649
Either way it's running on its own, they say

28
00:01:56,649 --> 00:02:01,915
Either way, nobody's name is on the page

29
00:02:01,915 --> 00:02:05,186
Three hundred words over a White House lunch

30
00:02:05,186 --> 00:02:09,894
"Morally binding" — no regulator, no punch

31
00:02:09,894 --> 00:02:13,723
They'll pick their own auditors, they'll grade their own test

32
00:02:13,723 --> 00:02:17,952
And one hand that signed it funds a PAC to fight the rest

33
00:02:17,952 --> 00:02:20,106
Who wrote the prompt? (Who wrote the prompt?)

34
00:02:20,106 --> 00:02:22,181
Who set the score?

35
00:02:22,181 --> 00:02:26,410
Who grades the test, and who keeps the door?

36
00:02:26,410 --> 00:02:30,160
It's not a demon, it's not a god

37
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:36,622
Ask who's holding it — and who writes the law

38
00:02:36,622 --> 00:02:39,087
This song was written with Claude.

39
00:02:39,387 --> 00:02:42,675
Every opinion in it is mine.

40
00:02:42,975 --> 00:02:45,807
So is the prompt.
